module coroutine.sus.spi

--[[
`coroutine.sus.spi` defines the scheduler integration contracts.

```nupp
local contract = coroutine.sus.spi
local type Provider = contract.Provider
```


Importing these declarations initializes no scheduler.
The facade retains the selected functions. Source, Context, Waiting, Handler,
and Installed are the shared types; providers initialize these declarations or
satisfy their exact signatures without replacing their nominal identities.

Each record declares what its holder may read and nothing else. Whatever state an
implementation needs beside that is its own, kept where callers cannot reach it,
so two implementations may represent a source or an installation differently and
neither has to reproduce the other's layout.

A subscription may resume synchronously or later. It must settle a Waiting only
once and run returned cleanup when the wait ends, including cancellation.
`Waiting.onresume` is settle-safe: registering a waker on a wait that has already
settled runs it immediately. Source release and Installed close must not suspend.
Nested installation restores the captured handler, and a driver installation
preserves delegation to the outer scheduler. `create` propagates the suspension
context into a new coroutine.

Sources report readiness in `order`, lowest first. Context.uses identifies
sources needed by a wait. Whether a park is permitted here is `cansuspend`,
which returns for the handler in force. Cancellation values must come from
[](coroutine.sus.cancellation), which preserves recognition by tasks and
worker providers. State belongs to one Lua state; registrations and handlers are
not copied into worker lanes.
]]
local source1 = require("nupp.suspension.spi")
export type Context = source1.Context
export type Create<A..., R...> = source1.Create<A..., R...>
export type Handler = source1.Handler
export type Installed = source1.Installed
export type Provider = source1.Provider
export type Source = source1.Source
export type Suspend<T> = source1.Suspend<T>
export type Waiting = source1.Waiting
export const Context = source1.Context
export const Handler = source1.Handler
export const Installed = source1.Installed
export const Source = source1.Source
export const Waiting = source1.Waiting
